{
  "exp_id": "EXP-2",
  "title": "Medium dataset: where a single node gives out",
  "hypothesis": "The single-node pandas configuration (B2) is the first to fail as the data grows, while the Spark configuration (B3) keeps going.",
  "independent_variable": "dataset size (customers), configuration",
  "dependent_measures": [
    "completed",
    "wall_clock_s",
    "peak_rss_mb",
    "bytes_on_disk",
    "rows_trained",
    "test_pr_auc"
  ],
  "started_at": "2026-10-08T16:17:15.764056+00:00",
  "duration_s": 1870.99,
  "status": "partial",
  "hypothesis_held": false,
  "conclusion": "Ladder: 400 customers, 0.4 MB on disk: B2 ok in 11s, B3 ok in 82s; 1500 customers, 1.4 MB on disk: B2 ok in 9s, B3 ok in 67s; 6000 customers, 5.1 MB on disk: B2 ok in 11s, B3 ok in 67s; 20000 customers, 14.9 MB on disk: B2 ok in 22s, B3 ok in 126s; 50000 customers, 36.4 MB on disk: B2 ok in 39s, B3 ok in 226s; 100000 customers: generating the data itself failed (experiments.exp02_medium_dataset:generate ended after 570s without returning (exit code -9); the container's cgroup recorded 1 out-of-memory kill(s) meanwhile). No crossover was observed within the sizes this machine can hold, so the hypothesis is neither supported nor refuted here. At the largest rung both completed (customers_50000), B2 took 39.3s and B3 226.2s, with peak memory 1240.8 MB for B2's Python process and 2186.2 MB for B3's Spark JVM. The PRD's 10 GB tier is not reported: see the limitations. Configuration P is not on this ladder either - it is measured against B3 in EXP-1, where the comparison is at a size all three can complete.",
  "limitations": [
    "The PRD's 10 GB tier was not run and is not estimated. Docker has a 5.27 GB VM here and the sandbox clamps any container to 3 GB (ADR-0002), so a 10 GB dataset would fail for every configuration including the ones the hypothesis expects to finish - three failures and no information. What is measured instead is the crossover the hypothesis asserts: the rung at which B2 stops and B3 does not.",
    "REES46 monthly files were not used. The project has no network access for dataset downloads in this environment and large datasets must not be committed to git.",
    "The ladder stopped at 100000 customers because generating the dataset exceeded what the container holds (experiments.exp02_medium_dataset:generate ended after 570s without returning (exit code -9); the container's cgroup recorded 1 out-of-memory kill(s) meanwhile); neither configuration was run on it."
  ],
